{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_28a390ed4616a085c05558bea2c20495b5f70a3aa95d208eb196e26f2b162aa0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Requires Neovim 0.10+ and a globally installed pi binary, installed via a curl script; models must be available in pi."},{"claim_ids":["clm_51a9c1b91ad342590ec9159e66c0fad19de7bc4aa6eb16e11e3a7710982eb3e6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Setting a custom system_prompt overrides pi's generated baseline instructions, which the README flags as something to use with care."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5b36b0ea4a337697cb3b8da3f5f2956ba55038e9f6355dc951a6aabf620967bd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Status updates use nvim-notify or mini.notify when available, falling back to a floating status window otherwise."},{"claim_ids":["clm_62ad7e0089384df6254c03da4eb470dacf1fc945e1bed692886c4dcb1aed1a3f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tools option lets users restrict pi's tools; read, edit, and write are always enabled, and an empty list disables bash."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6618eb0df2f2fd1ff23c07c8c861a578638e68cc71e2fc064fed57c622218136"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The plugin wraps the external pi CLI binary (default \"pi\", configurable to a custom path or wrapper command array) rather than implementing the agent itself."},{"claim_ids":["clm_69a750720892e130c64a1c2becf3f1138e584f8770b09cf3532caa2634c0953e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Requests run asynchronously so editing stays nonblocking, and changed loaded buffers are reloaded after successful pi edits."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a4fe14f010e1d0b7237efcdaac5abdd9fc6c503e8d1d25323645ee0c79e65e94"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The plugin exposes four user commands: :PiAsk (normal mode, prompts and sends buffer context), :PiAskSelection (visual), :PiCancel, and :PiLog which opens a session log split."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a7db40426f031c7e0e8272dc339cf8e356cfd0a106f3e1396a92f06ee7fb8f4a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A Lua setup API is documented via require(\"pi\").setup with all options optional, plus programmatic get_cmd() and run() functions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bb1cd15dba29e82634dbb26b02229ed71cc9bab73fa7bb46298fd724c3a57c5d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Oversized context is trimmed (default max 24000 bytes) for speed rather than always sending the full file."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d77bfa6588d952a8cbbe61cce0cd8d11581593368eb685a00d10818ad53f2ddc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration options include binary path, provider, model, thinking level (off through xhigh), tools list, system prompts, and context sizing knobs like max_bytes and surrounding_lines."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e3d7c9a0bafda0c239d62511456a473786c1c82887005c5f7070fe56e0d8780a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"No default keymaps are set; users configure their own, with example mappings for :PiAsk and :PiAskSelection provided."},{"claim_ids":["clm_eabac3ec142aeca91f8738484861ea3c1896c9a0de38ff28044478d7cbad3ca9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Context sent to pi includes the current buffer, cwd, selection, and optionally LSP/linter diagnostics via vim.diagnostic, with unsaved buffer content treated as the source of truth over disk."}],"claim_ids":["clm_28a390ed4616a085c05558bea2c20495b5f70a3aa95d208eb196e26f2b162aa0","clm_51a9c1b91ad342590ec9159e66c0fad19de7bc4aa6eb16e11e3a7710982eb3e6","clm_5b36b0ea4a337697cb3b8da3f5f2956ba55038e9f6355dc951a6aabf620967bd","clm_62ad7e0089384df6254c03da4eb470dacf1fc945e1bed692886c4dcb1aed1a3f","clm_6618eb0df2f2fd1ff23c07c8c861a578638e68cc71e2fc064fed57c622218136","clm_69a750720892e130c64a1c2becf3f1138e584f8770b09cf3532caa2634c0953e","clm_a4fe14f010e1d0b7237efcdaac5abdd9fc6c503e8d1d25323645ee0c79e65e94","clm_a7db40426f031c7e0e8272dc339cf8e356cfd0a106f3e1396a92f06ee7fb8f4a","clm_bb1cd15dba29e82634dbb26b02229ed71cc9bab73fa7bb46298fd724c3a57c5d","clm_d77bfa6588d952a8cbbe61cce0cd8d11581593368eb685a00d10818ad53f2ddc","clm_e3d7c9a0bafda0c239d62511456a473786c1c82887005c5f7070fe56e0d8780a","clm_eabac3ec142aeca91f873848486